epdcl vegetation_conductor # Vegetation–Conductor Segmentation Module - PD-Defect

Collection, licensing, and citation are documented on the [main dataset card](../README.md).

## TL;DR

Semantic segmentation of vegetation and conductors in distribution scenes. Annotations are COCO polygons (`1 = Conductor`, `2 = Vegetation`) that rasterize to per-class masks. The release contains 1,781 images (1,324 train (74.34%) / 457 validation (25.66%)) and has no test split. An image-level Risky / Safe Ground Truth file is provided for the validation split. Thin low-contrast conductors, occlusion, and severe class imbalance are present in the data.

## Task Definition

Segment vegetation and conductors at the pixel level.

## Label Definitions

- **Vegetation:** trees, branches, leaves, and other plant structure within the conductor corridor or its immediate vicinity relevant to clearance assessment (see Annotation Protocol).
- **Conductor:** electrical conductors associated with distribution infrastructure
- **Background:** all regions not covered by a Conductor or Vegetation polygon (implicit; not separately annotated)

The masks define regions only. They do not encode distance or clearance risk. Risk labels are prov
